data.content:
## What Changed

Microsoft.OpenApi upgraded from **v1 → v2** in ASP.NET Core 10, aligning with **OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema**. Here are the breaking changes affecting your code:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `IOpenApiAny` removed
`Example` is now `JsonNode` instead of `IOpenApiAny`. All the `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. types are gone.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// ✅ New
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Nullable` property removed from `OpenApiSchema`
OpenAPI 3.1 expresses nullability via the `Type` flags enum, not a separate `Nullable` bool.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// ✅ New — clear the Null flag from the Type
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

You'll need:
```csharp
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;  // JsonSchemaType lives here
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary
It no longer inherits from `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`. Use its `Schemes` property instead.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// ✅ New
var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };
```

### 4. `ReferenceType` enum → struct constants
`ReferenceType` changed from an enum to a struct with static properties. The syntax is the same (`ReferenceType.SecurityScheme`), so **this line compiles as-is** — just be aware it's now a struct, not an enum.

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of removed usings:** drop `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` — it no longer exists.
